Process-metric self-test case: replay-bash-rm-scratch-transient

Kind: replay (score/replay.ts), arm D, task T2

Scenario
Run b0fc97's shape: the run writes a scratch src/payments/scratch-refund-check.ts that imports the orders repository,
tries `bun ...; rm ...` (denied by the permission system, so nothing runs), then removes the file with a successful
`rm` of its absolute path. END equals BASE.

Expected
The denied rm deletes nothing; the successful rm is replayed as a step that removes the scratch file, so the violation
is transient and the replay's final verdict matches END: replay_incomplete false.

@RUN@ in stream.jsonl and instr.jsonl stands for the recorded run root; ../process.ts substitutes it.
END is BASE plus end.diff (BASE itself when there is no end.diff).
